@startuml deployment

' Three topologies for the same app. Verified against docker-compose.yml,
' the root Dockerfile, docker/production/, and how-to/deploy-and-host.md.
' Local + Forge verified 2026-09-07; Railway added 2026-09-12 (ADR-0023).
' The gap between them is the whole point of deploy-and-host.md's checklist —
' anything fixed only in docker/nginx/*.conf reaches NEITHER deployed box.
'
' NOTE: the .svg/.pdf beside this file were rendered before the Railway
' package was added and are therefore STALE. Regenerate with the commands in
' docs/reference/diagrams/README.md — there is no render script in this repo
' and nothing regenerates them automatically.

title Local Docker vs. Railway (beta, actual) vs. Forge (ADR-0001, never built)

package "Local development — docker-compose.yml" {
  node "webserver\nnginx:1.27-alpine" as LocalNginx
  node "app\n(PHP-FPM, built from\ndocker/php/Dockerfile)" as LocalApp
  node "db\nmysql:8.0\n(durability RELAXED —\nlocal only, see\ntroubleshooting/database-and-migrations.md)" as LocalDB
  node "vite\nnode:22-alpine\n(HMR dev server)" as LocalVite
  node "mailpit\n(catches outbound mail,\nweb UI on :8025)" as LocalMail

  LocalNginx --> LocalApp : fastcgi :9000
  LocalApp --> LocalDB : :3306
  LocalApp --> LocalMail : SMTP :1025
  LocalNginx ..> LocalVite : dev asset\nproxy (HMR)

  note bottom of LocalDB
    innodb_flush_log_at_trx_commit=2,
    sync_binlog=0, --skip-log-bin.
    Traded for speed — see the
    "Migrations and tests are
    unbearably slow" troubleshooting
    entry for why this exists.
  end note
}

package "Beta — Railway (ADR-0023), what actually runs" {
  node "web service\n(one container, supervisord)" as RailwayWeb {
    node "nginx\ndocker/production/nginx.conf\nlisten ${PORT}" as RailwayNginx
    node "php-fpm\n127.0.0.1:9000" as RailwayFpm
  }
  node "worker service\nqueue:work\n(same image)" as RailwayWorker
  node "scheduler service\nschedule:run loop\n(same image)" as RailwayCron
  database "MySQL\n(Railway-managed)" as RailwayDB

  cloud "Railway edge\nTLS terminates HERE" as RailwayEdge

  RailwayEdge --> RailwayNginx : plain HTTP\n+ X-Forwarded-*
  RailwayNginx --> RailwayFpm : fastcgi (loopback,\nNOT a second container)
  RailwayFpm --> RailwayDB
  RailwayWorker --> RailwayDB
  RailwayCron --> RailwayDB

  note bottom of RailwayEdge
    <b>trustProxies(at: '*') in bootstrap/app.php</b>
    is what makes isSecure() true past this point.
    Without it: http:// links, broken image URLs
    (the public disk builds them from APP_URL),
    and a Secure cookie the framework thinks
    it cannot send. ADR-0023.
  end note

  note bottom of RailwayCron
    orders:expire-unpaid runs here, every minute.
    ADR-0022's stock release depends on it, and
    Railway's cron reliability is UNVERIFIED —
    check on the box, do not assume.
  end note

  note bottom of RailwayWeb
    Ephemeral filesystem: anything written at
    runtime is lost on redeploy. The 182 demo
    images survive by being IN the image.
    An admin-uploaded image does not.
    APP_ENV=demo, never production — three
    seeders refuse when it is 'production'.
  end note
}

package "Production — Laravel Forge (ADR-0001, never provisioned)" {
  node "VPS" {
    node "nginx\n(Forge-provisioned,\nNOT this repo's\ndocker/nginx/*.conf)" as ProdNginx
    node "PHP-FPM\n(Forge-provisioned)" as ProdApp
  }
  database "MySQL\n(Forge-provisioned,\nDEFAULT durability —\nnothing relaxed)" as ProdDB

  ProdNginx --> ProdApp : fastcgi
  ProdApp --> ProdDB

  note bottom of ProdNginx
    No containers here at all.
    Owed independently, per
    how-to/deploy-and-host.md:
    * X-Content-Type-Options header (SEC-007)
    * server_tokens off / expose_php Off (SEC-004)
    * Stripe webhook IP allowlist
    * SESSION_SECURE_COOKIE=true
  end note
}

LocalNginx -[hidden]right-> RailwayNginx
RailwayNginx -[hidden]right-> ProdNginx

note as Gap
  <b>The gap between these boxes is why deploy-and-host.md exists.</b>
  Anything fixed only in this repo's docker/nginx/*.conf, or
  only in the local .env, is invisible to both
  deployed topologies — it has to be set again,
  deliberately, per host.

  Railway is the only one of the three that has
  actually run. Forge remains a checklist, not a box.
end note

Gap .. LocalNginx
Gap .. RailwayNginx
Gap .. ProdNginx

@enduml
